{"parents": [{"link": "../", "title": "Available Methods"}], "prev": {"link": "../invoke/", "title": "invoke()"}, "next": {"link": "../get_file/", "title": "get_file()"}, "title": "resolve_peer()", "meta": null, "body": "<section id=\"resolve-peer\">\n<h1>resolve_peer()<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#resolve-peer\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyrogram.Client.resolve_peer\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">Client.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">resolve_peer</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#pyrogram.Client.resolve_peer\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get the InputPeer of a known peer id.\nUseful whenever an InputPeer type is required.</p>\n<div class=\"admonition note\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Note</p>\n<p>This is a utility method intended to be used <strong>only</strong> when working with raw\n<code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">functions</span></code> (i.e: a Telegram API method you wish to use which is not\navailable yet in the Client class as an easy-to-use method).</p>\n</div>\n<strong>Usable by</strong>\n<span class=\"usable-by\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-check\" style=\"color: var(--color-green)\"></i> Users</span>\n<span class=\"usable-by\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-check\" style=\"color: var(--color-green)\"></i> Bots</span><dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>peer_id</strong> (<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></code> | <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></code>) \u2013 The peer id you want to extract the InputPeer from.\nCan be a direct id (int), a username (str) or a phone number (str).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">InputPeer</span></code> \u2013 On success, the resolved peer id is returned in form of an InputPeer object.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Raises<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/library/exceptions.html#KeyError\" title=\"(in Python v3.14)\"><strong>KeyError</strong></a> \u2013 In case the peer doesn\u2019t exist in the internal database.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n", "metatags": "<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n", "rellinks": [["genindex", "General Index", "I", "index"], ["py-modindex", "Python Module Index", "", "modules"], ["api/methods/get_file", "get_file()", "N", "next"], ["api/methods/invoke", "invoke()", "P", "previous"]], "sourcename": "", "toc": "<ul>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#\">resolve_peer()</a><ul>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#pyrogram.Client.resolve_peer\"><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Client.resolve_peer()</span></code></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n", "display_toc": true, "page_source_suffix": ".rst", "current_page_name": "api/methods/resolve_peer", "sidebars": ["sidebar/brand.html", "sidebar/search.html", "sidebar/scroll-start.html", "sidebar/navigation.html", "sidebar/scroll-end.html"], "alabaster_version": "1.0.0", "alabaster_version_info": [1, 0, 0], "furo_version": "2025.12.19", "furo_navigation_tree": "", "furo_hide_toc": false, "furo_pygments": {"light": {"background": "#eeffcc", "foreground": "black"}, "dark": {"background": "#202020", "foreground": "#d0d0d0"}}}